Yes, this is completely clear. Stripping away the conversational wording, this is a **2-Level Binary Matrix / Foodstuff Network Marketing (MLM) platform**.

It follows the classic Nigerian "food empowerment / agro-cooperative" referral model: deposit registration capital, bring 2 direct downlines (binary matrix split: left and right), cycle out to collect physical food packages (rice, oil, provisions, etc.), and optionally re-enter the pool.

---

### Core Mechanics & User Flow

```
[User Signs Up via Referral Link]
             │
             ▼
[Deposit Stage: View Admin Bank Details]
             │
             ▼
[Upload Proof of Payment / Automated Paystack/Moniepoint Virtual Account]
             │
             ▼
[Admin Approves / Auto-Verify: Account Activated]
             │
             ▼
[User Refers Person A + Person B (2 Downlines Complete Matrix)]
             │
             ▼
[Eligibility Met: Foodstuff Incentive Dispatched / Claim Code Issued]
             │
             ▼
[Re-entry Loop: Cycle Out or Pay to Rejoin]

```

---

### Functional Components Required

#### 1. Public & Onboarding Flow

* **Registration with Referral Binding:** User signs up (`Full Name`, `Phone`, `Email`, `Username`, `Password`). If arriving via a link like `[site.com/register?ref=username](https://site.com/register?ref=username)`, lock the upline username into the form.
* **Referral Guardrails:** If no referral link is used, assign a default system admin upline to prevent orphan nodes in the tree.

#### 2. Member Portal

* **Dashboard:** Shows activation status (*Inactive / Active / Cycled Out*), personal referral link, and direct downline count ($0/2$).
* **Deposit / Payment Section:**
* Displays the company bank details (Bank name, Account Number, Account Name).
* Proof of Payment (POP) upload field (screenshot/transaction receipt) with transfer reference or automated virtual account payment.


* **Binary Referral Tree / Matrix View:** Visual or list breakdown of their two assigned children (Downline 1 and Downline 2) and their payment statuses.
* **Reward / Entitlement Status:** Shows milestone completion (e.g., *“Target Reached: Eligible for Foodstuff Package A”*), redemption status (*Pending Dispatch / Collected*), and a “Re-enter / Rejoin” button.

#### 3. Admin Control Center

* **Payment Verification Queue:** Table showing member name, amount, bank reference, uploaded receipt image, and action buttons (*Approve* / *Decline*).
* **Referral Tree & Cycle Management:** Tracks users who have completed their $1 \rightarrow 2$ matrix requirements to trigger reward dispatches.
* **Foodstuff Inventory & Fulfillment Desk:** Marks food packages as *Prepared*, *Shipped*, or *Redeemed via Pickup Center/Agent*.
* **Re-entry Engine:** Clones/resets the user node to re-enter a new matrix upon new deposit confirmation.

